# The buzz commit this deployment is built and tested against.
#
# We do NOT fork buzz. Our clone is a pure consumer (zero tracked
# modifications, verified 2026-08-02), so a fork would buy a permanent merge
# burden for a capability we have never used. Instead we pin, and bumping the
# pin is a reviewed diff like any other.
#
# Bump procedure:
#   1. git -C <buzz clone> fetch && git log --oneline <old>..<new>
#   2. Read deploy/compose/compose.yml for changes to the relay service —
#      that file is the surface our overlay layers onto.
#   3. Update REF + DESCRIBE below, rebuild, redeploy to staging, smoke.
#   4. Commit with the upstream range in the message.
REF=ac4fa13b8e4d947071d57deb6918dcf12bf74961
DESCRIBE=desktop-v0.5.3-17-gac4fa13b8
DATE=2026-08-01T13:32:16-04:00
SUBJECT=perf(relay): serve relay-membership checks from the read replica (#4124)

# Where a server can actually fetch it. Our dev clone's origin is
# /Volumes/<workspace>/mirrors/buzz.git — a LOCAL mirror, unreachable from a
# droplet — so builds off-box must use this URL instead.
#
# Verified 2026-08-02, not inferred from the ghcr image name:
#   * anonymous `git ls-remote https://github.com/block/buzz HEAD` exits 0,
#     so the droplet needs no deploy key;
#   * the mirror's ONLY remote is git@github.com:block/buzz, so every commit
#     in it originated there;
#   * REF below is contained in the mirror's refs/heads/main, i.e. it is an
#     ancestor of GitHub's main and can actually be checked out remotely.
#     (A pin present only in a local mirror would fail at deploy, not here.)
#
# Use the HTTPS form. On the dev Macs a global `insteadOf` rewrites HTTPS to
# SSH, so a local clone may transparently go over SSH; a droplet has no such
# rewrite and the repo is public, so HTTPS is correct there.
UPSTREAM_URL=https://github.com/block/buzz
